Duel Draft D2 §7.1 — budget-monotonicity diagnostic (POST-DUCT re-run, C66/C73)
seed="duel-draft-d2-71-monotonicity", games=30/budget, candidates=[1000, 2000, 5000, 10000]
Watching for the C55 signature: strong-vs-random DECLINING as budget rises.

rollouts=  1000  strong-vs-random win rate = 73.3%  (SE ~8.1 pts, n=30)  drawRate=26.7%  meanPlies=6.6  capHitRate=0.00%
rollouts=  2000  strong-vs-random win rate = 76.7%  (SE ~7.7 pts, n=30)  drawRate=23.3%  meanPlies=6.4  capHitRate=0.00%
rollouts=  5000  strong-vs-random win rate = 86.7%  (SE ~6.2 pts, n=30)  drawRate=13.3%  meanPlies=6.2  capHitRate=0.00%
rollouts= 10000  strong-vs-random win rate = 76.7%  (SE ~7.7 pts, n=30)  drawRate=23.3%  meanPlies=6.6  capHitRate=0.00%

=== Pairwise deltas (rate[i+1] - rate[i], in points) — CONTEXT ONLY, NOT the verdict ===
(unpaired binomial SE — the wrong error model for this paired-seed design; see C75. The
 VERDICT below is derived from the paired McNemar exact test further down, not from this.)
  1000 -> 2000: +3.3 pts (combined SE ~11.2 pts) => flat/rose
  2000 -> 5000: +10.0 pts (combined SE ~9.9 pts) => flat/rose
  5000 -> 10000: -10.0 pts (combined SE ~9.9 pts) => declined beyond naive SE band

=== Paired per-index transitions (same seed/games across candidates — the correct error model) ===
  1000 -> 2000: 21 unchanged, 5 flipped TO a strong win, 4 flipped AWAY from a strong win (net +1), McNemar exact p=1.0000
  2000 -> 5000: 23 unchanged, 5 flipped TO a strong win, 2 flipped AWAY from a strong win (net +3), McNemar exact p=0.4531
  5000 -> 10000: 25 unchanged, 1 flipped TO a strong win, 4 flipped AWAY from a strong win (net -3), McNemar exact p=0.3750

=== VERDICT (derived from the paired McNemar exact test above, alpha=0.05) ===
No pairwise decline is significant under the paired McNemar exact test (alpha=0.05) — no C55 signature on this seed/n by this measure. Duel Draft control stays non-declining post-DUCT.
